<title>UK: Railtrack shares squeezed up to new high.</title>
<headline>Railtrack shares squeezed up to new high.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Railtrack Plc defied a weaker to market to hit a new record on Friday, squeezed up by a shortage of stock, dealers said.</p>
<p>The shares reached a record 460p and were up 11-1/2 at 457 by 1243 GMT.</p>
<p>&quot;It's very, very squeezy,&quot; one market-maker said. &quot;There were a couple of big buyers early on and people found themselves short of stock.&quot;</p>
<p>The shares received a boost last week from a 15.9 billion stg plan unveiled by the company.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8712</p>
